In article <1994Jan20.203041.2344@Informatik.TU-Muenchen.DE>, millert@Informatik.TU-Muenchen.DE (Tobias Miller) writes:

>i'm trying to make Nethack-3.1.3 run on HPUX. No problems during compilation,
>but after having startet the game, no dungeon appears. Everything else works
>fine, just the TTY-Graphics are not displayed. (I can even move around the
>screen, hit monster, activate all commands etc...)
>Do i have to change the config.h unixconf.h & Makefiles ?
>What configurations are needed ?
>Any hints are welcome.

I've compiled for TTY with HPUX.  Here is a list of all the things I changed
(less the things I changed trying to get the X11 version working):


Makefile:18:GAMEUID  = snelling
Makefile:35:GAMEDIR  = /bnr/users/u3/snelling/public/$(GAME)dir
Makefile:36:SHELLDIR = /bnr/users/u3/snelling/bin

doc/Makefile:24:MANDIR  = /bnr/users/u3/snelling/man/man6
include/config.h:110:#define TERMINFO   /* uses terminfo rather than termcap */
include/config.h:239:#  define WIZARD  "snelling" /* the person allowed to use the -D option */
include/config.h:242:#  define WIZARD_NAME "snelling"
include/config.h:265:# define COMPRESS "/usr/bin/compress"           /* Lempel-Ziv compression */
include/config.h:292:#define HACKDIR "/bnr/users/u3/snelling/public/nethack3.1.3dir"    /* nethack directory *
include/unixconf.h:22:/* #define BSD            /* define for 4.n BSD */
include/unixconf.h:28:#define HPUX      /* Hewlett-Packard's Unix, version 6.5 or higher */
include/unixconf.h:36:/* #define SUNOS4 /* SunOS 4.x */
include/unixconf.h:44:#define TEXTCOLOR /*  Use System V r3.2 terminfo color support */
include/unixconf.h:110:/* #define MAIL       /* Deliver mail during the game */
src/Makefile:153:LIBS = -l malloc 
src/Makefile:156:GAME     = nethack3.1.3 

